	(text "This is a TED Magic Voice cartridge. It is\nbased on the circuit in the Commodore V364\nprototype. It uses a custom Gate Array\nchip that replaced the 6525TPI, LA05-124 and\nTTL chips in the C64 Magic Voice. It has a\nROM socket that supports various capacities\nand configurations.\n\nThe TED series PLA chip has an unused \"F0\"\npin which is for the Gate Array. You must\nconnect Pin 17 of the Gate Array to the\nF0 connector on the cartridge.\n\n*** IMPORTANT:\n*** This PCB is a prototype to help in\n*** developing a replacement drop-in\n*** Gate Array chip for the V364 Remake!!!\n*** It is NOT complete or tested!"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 13.716 161.798 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.524 1.524)
				(thickness 0.3048)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left)
		)
		(uuid "04c5ad83-f559-4c75-8d56-d729fd057d58")
	)
